# CatDex — Database Schema

## Core tables (`supabase/schema.sql`)

| Table | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `profiles` | Extends `auth.users` |
| `cats` | Owned captures (geo, dex_number, photo_url, …) |
| `sightings` | Sightings linked to cats |
| `cat_analysis` | 1:1 analysis payload |
| `analysis_feedback` | User corrections / training signal |

Extensions: `uuid-ossp`, `postgis`. Geography points for map queries.

## Rules

- Additive migrations preferred (`ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS`, safe policy drops/recreates)
- Keep RLS enabled; update policies in the same PR as schema changes
- Indexes: owner, created_at, dex_number, GiST on geography
- App models in `src/types/cat.ts` may be richer than columns — map carefully in sync layer
- Never invent parallel shadow databases in the client

## When changing schema

1. Update `supabase/migrations/` (and schema snapshot if that’s the project practice)
2. Update sync/queries
3. Document backfill needs in the PR
